WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:04.364
- What's up Believe nation?

00:00:04.364 --> 00:00:06.415
I used to get sick a lot,

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:08.864
I used to believe that if I
didn't eat the right foods

00:00:08.864 --> 00:00:10.629
I would get sick, that if I didn't sleep

00:00:10.629 --> 00:00:12.526
the right number of
hours I would get sick,

00:00:12.526 --> 00:00:15.801
that if anybody around me was
sick then I would get sick,

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:17.425
and guess what happened?

00:00:17.425 --> 00:00:20.839
I got sick a lot, and then
in January of this year

00:00:20.839 --> 00:00:22.578
after getting really sick I decided

00:00:22.578 --> 00:00:24.679
I am never going to get sick again.

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:27.516
Never sick again, I'm
always going to be healthy

00:00:27.516 --> 00:00:30.434
and dedicated myself to learning
from some of the masters.

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.346
People who have figured
it out for themselves

00:00:32.346 --> 00:00:34.295
on how to never get sick

00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:38.152
so that also spawned this
new series called Never Sick

00:00:38.152 --> 00:00:40.886
and today we're going to learn
from Wim Hof, the ice man,

00:00:40.886 --> 00:00:43.636
on his techniques, his
strategies, his secrets

00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:45.757
to never get sick,

00:00:45.757 --> 00:00:47.498
and as always guys as Wim is talking

00:00:47.498 --> 00:00:49.641
if he says something that
really resonates with you

00:00:49.641 --> 00:00:51.262
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:51.262 --> 00:00:53.946
put quotes around it so
others can enjoy it as well.

00:00:53.946 --> 00:00:56.529
(upbeat music)

00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:01.562
(mysterious music)

00:01:10.581 --> 00:01:14.578
- [Wim] To me God is
cold, you could say that.

00:01:14.578 --> 00:01:17.600
I think of the cold as a noble force,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.747
it's just helping me, it's training me,

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.376
it's bringing me back to the inner nature

00:01:23.376 --> 00:01:25.626
the way it was meant to be,

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:31.130
and this way I do not
only endure the cold,

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.463
I love the cold.

00:01:33.951 --> 00:01:37.118
(deep slow breathing)

00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:52.206
(electronic music)

00:01:57.337 --> 00:01:59.489
- We live in a world
where there's all kinds

00:01:59.489 --> 00:02:02.967
of false healers and fake
alternative medicine programs

00:02:02.967 --> 00:02:04.650
you can sign up for.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.392
It's a rare moment in history
when someone comes along

00:02:07.392 --> 00:02:09.425
who can perform real miracles

00:02:09.425 --> 00:02:11.811
with real evidence to back them up.

00:02:11.811 --> 00:02:15.360
Wim Hof has defied logic
time and time again

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.275
and always under scientific scrutiny.

00:02:18.275 --> 00:02:19.338
He holds the world record

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:22.545
for being able to be submerged
in ice for almost two hours

00:02:22.545 --> 00:02:24.773
without his core body
temperature changing.

00:02:24.773 --> 00:02:27.711
He's climbed Mount Everest in
nothing but a pair of shorts

00:02:27.711 --> 00:02:31.429
and ran a marathon in the desert
without drinking any water.

00:02:31.429 --> 00:02:33.676
He's even proven in a laboratory setting

00:02:33.676 --> 00:02:38.056
that he can withstand illnesses
using the power of his mind,

00:02:38.056 --> 00:02:39.795
but he's not a freak of nature.

00:02:39.795 --> 00:02:42.731
According to Wim anyone
can do what he can do.

00:02:42.731 --> 00:02:47.026
They just have to learn his
method, the Wim Hof Method,

00:02:47.026 --> 00:02:49.067
using a combination of cold immersion,

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:52.313
breathing techniques and mental focus

00:02:52.313 --> 00:02:54.106
anyone can accomplish feats

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:57.939
that were previously
thought to be impossible.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:18.977
- I created a method, the
components are breathing,

00:03:20.595 --> 00:03:22.845
mind set and cold exposure,

00:03:23.883 --> 00:03:26.633
gradual non-forced cold exposure,

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:32.602
and that's to optimize
the mind body connection.

00:03:32.602 --> 00:03:35.469
- Wim has figured out ways,
namely through breath work

00:03:35.469 --> 00:03:38.671
and through exposure to cold
to take conscious control

00:03:38.671 --> 00:03:43.133
over aspects of his physiology
that for most people

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:46.463
they simply can't tune into and control.

00:03:46.463 --> 00:03:48.233
(wind blowing)

00:03:48.233 --> 00:03:50.764
(piano music)

00:03:50.764 --> 00:03:53.527
- The cold, my warm friend,

00:03:53.527 --> 00:03:55.970
it brings about a whole lot of more energy

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:59.010
and that together with breathing

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.093
makes you so powerful but
then you lose your wife

00:04:03.953 --> 00:04:05.953
and it all rumbles down.

00:04:08.996 --> 00:04:11.830
Four children I had with my wife

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.580
and I was to be with her forever.

00:04:16.104 --> 00:04:19.712
She was the love of my life, she died.

00:04:19.712 --> 00:04:20.795
She suicided.

00:04:22.297 --> 00:04:25.130
It's a black hole within yourself.

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:28.967
It breaks your heart
and you don't know why

00:04:28.967 --> 00:04:32.435
but the train of daily life is going on

00:04:32.435 --> 00:04:35.452
and you got to catch up
otherwise you lose it

00:04:35.452 --> 00:04:38.923
so I had to be there
for my children and yes,

00:04:38.923 --> 00:04:41.476
we created a new nest.

00:04:41.476 --> 00:04:45.400
My children made me survive in that time,

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.733
but nature healed my wounds.

00:04:50.412 --> 00:04:55.396
The cold gave me a direct
understanding of deeper breathing

00:04:55.396 --> 00:04:58.234
and how to heal a broken heart.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:01.928
Then I went and did all kinds
of remarkable challenges.

00:05:01.928 --> 00:05:05.676
Apparently they found it
very remarkable and great

00:05:05.676 --> 00:05:09.034
and spectacular so I came
in contact with television.

00:05:09.034 --> 00:05:11.544
One after the other they
challenged me more, more,

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.735
more, more, more.

00:05:12.735 --> 00:05:15.605
"Hey go swim 50 meters under the ice.

00:05:15.605 --> 00:05:18.217
"Go and swim 100 meters under the ice.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.052
"Climb Mount Everest in shorts."

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:24.052
That led up, that the
scientists became curious.

00:05:25.456 --> 00:05:27.146
"Hey what this man is doing

00:05:27.146 --> 00:05:29.979
"is not possible physiologically."

00:05:32.383 --> 00:05:34.414
- The science of what Wim Hof Method does

00:05:34.414 --> 00:05:36.917
is one of the primary
interests of my lab now

00:05:36.917 --> 00:05:38.038
because it is so powerful

00:05:38.038 --> 00:05:40.348
and it's been shown to be
powerful in the immune system.

00:05:40.348 --> 00:05:43.083
We believe it will also
hold some real potential

00:05:43.083 --> 00:05:46.148
for treatment of neurological diseases.

00:05:46.148 --> 00:05:48.912
- [Wim] And this breathing
technique brings you right into

00:05:48.912 --> 00:05:52.487
the deepest part of
physiology, anybody can do it.

00:05:52.487 --> 00:05:56.654
So you become the alchemist
of your own chemistry.

00:05:58.064 --> 00:06:00.030
The first time I went under the ice

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:02.780
the water is as sharp as needles.

00:06:03.759 --> 00:06:07.009
I saw this as a big huge sharp diamond.

00:06:10.365 --> 00:06:12.448
At 35 meters I lost sight

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:18.196
because the retina, it froze,
I couldn't see nothing,

00:06:18.196 --> 00:06:22.521
I couldn't breathe of course
and then my consciousness

00:06:22.521 --> 00:06:26.688
succumbed to a lower
consciousness, this is survival.

00:06:28.471 --> 00:06:32.304
I do not fear death, I
fear not to live fully.

00:06:33.356 --> 00:06:37.273
If I live fully I'm not
into death, I'm living.

00:06:38.391 --> 00:06:40.819
- [Matt] It isn't all
about breaking records.

00:06:40.819 --> 00:06:43.975
Wim's mission is to use
his body as a laboratory,

00:06:43.975 --> 00:06:47.482
to revolutionize our
understanding of physiology.

00:06:47.482 --> 00:06:51.508
In 2011 he was injected
with a bacterial endotoxin

00:06:51.508 --> 00:06:52.939
in an experiment that challenged

00:06:52.939 --> 00:06:55.437
our understanding of the nervous system.

00:06:55.437 --> 00:06:57.228
In normal humans the injection

00:06:57.228 --> 00:06:59.671
should cause a strong immune response

00:06:59.671 --> 00:07:02.738
leading to fever, chills and headaches,

00:07:02.738 --> 00:07:04.424
but not in Wim.

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.938
It appeared that he was somehow able

00:07:05.938 --> 00:07:08.026
to suppress his immune response

00:07:08.026 --> 00:07:10.177
by making his body secrete adrenaline,

00:07:10.177 --> 00:07:13.899
suggesting that his method
can allow us to influence

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:16.526
our immune system at will.

00:07:16.526 --> 00:07:18.888
Scientists thought he might
just be a freak of nature

00:07:18.888 --> 00:07:20.752
so to further prove this theory

00:07:20.752 --> 00:07:22.671
they performed the same experiment

00:07:22.671 --> 00:07:25.350
on 12 subjects Wim had trained in Poland

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:28.054
and the same thing happened.

00:07:28.054 --> 00:07:29.317
- Normally it's very difficult

00:07:29.317 --> 00:07:33.239
to increase your adrenaline
levels by your own will.

00:07:33.239 --> 00:07:36.491
Adrenaline is released by
the autonomic nervous system

00:07:36.491 --> 00:07:40.020
and autonomic means that you
cannot voluntarily influence it

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.055
so if you walk outside and
you are robbed on the street

00:07:44.055 --> 00:07:47.366
you will have a heart rate of
160 and your blood pressure

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:50.069
will be sky high within seconds,

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:52.606
but if I ask you now to
increase your heart rate

00:07:52.606 --> 00:07:56.552
you cannot do that, you cannot
voluntarily modulate that,

00:07:56.552 --> 00:07:58.594
and with techniques of Wim Hof

00:07:58.594 --> 00:08:02.348
we show that he was able to
increase his adrenaline levels

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:04.145
to very high concentrations

00:08:04.145 --> 00:08:06.555
even higher than people
who go bungee jumping

00:08:06.555 --> 00:08:08.149
for the first time.

00:08:08.149 --> 00:08:10.651
That was something that
we didn't think possible

00:08:10.651 --> 00:08:11.651
before then.

00:08:12.851 --> 00:08:15.768
(electronic music)

00:08:21.275 --> 00:08:25.618
- Right now we are right
over here, 750 meters,

00:08:25.618 --> 00:08:29.857
we go up to 1,400 meters,
that's the Karpacz,

00:08:29.857 --> 00:08:31.913
from the Karpacz we go to the Sniezka

00:08:31.913 --> 00:08:35.413
and it's cold so all you have studied Matt

00:08:36.295 --> 00:08:38.056
you are going to need it

00:08:38.056 --> 00:08:41.082
and now just don't think, but focus,

00:08:41.082 --> 00:08:43.250
trust your body to be able to cope

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.791
with the elements up
there and you will be able

00:08:46.791 --> 00:08:49.277
and with that you are
going to show for yourself,

00:08:49.277 --> 00:08:51.832
"hey man I can do this, wow."

00:08:51.832 --> 00:08:54.749
(electronic music)

00:08:56.392 --> 00:08:58.557
- If you ever wanted a real test

00:08:58.557 --> 00:09:01.553
of the Wim Hof Method this is it.

00:09:01.553 --> 00:09:05.699
If you concentrate hard enough
the snow looks like sand

00:09:05.699 --> 00:09:07.413
and you just feel like
you're at the beach.

00:09:07.413 --> 00:09:09.152
- Exactly that's the mind,

00:09:09.152 --> 00:09:11.431
if your mind is on it,

00:09:11.431 --> 00:09:15.061
then you're quite capable of
dealing with the elements.

00:09:15.061 --> 00:09:17.430
- Yeah 'cause it is a bit nippy really.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:18.301
- Yeah.

00:09:18.301 --> 00:09:19.134
Hey.

00:09:19.134 --> 00:09:22.508
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:09:22.508 --> 00:09:25.675
(deep slow breathing)

00:09:37.294 --> 00:09:38.281
- There's a method to this,

00:09:38.281 --> 00:09:41.982
what I'm doing is breathing
in more oxygen than I need

00:09:41.982 --> 00:09:44.351
and then breathing out
without fully letting go.

00:09:44.351 --> 00:09:47.655
Doing that five times and
then on the final breath

00:09:47.655 --> 00:09:52.506
squeezing the oxygen into
your chest, neck and head

00:09:52.506 --> 00:09:56.506
and that creates either
real or illusionary heat

00:09:57.403 --> 00:09:59.455
and then you let go,

00:09:59.455 --> 00:10:01.122
and that's how we get to
the top of the mountain.

00:10:01.122 --> 00:10:03.926
Oh shit.
(laughing)

00:10:03.926 --> 00:10:04.926
My crampons.

00:10:07.972 --> 00:10:10.805
Minor crampon emergency, I'm fine.

00:10:12.627 --> 00:10:16.352
(deep slow breathing)

00:10:16.352 --> 00:10:18.028
There are a few theories

00:10:18.028 --> 00:10:22.065
as to why Wim Hof can do what he can do.

00:10:22.065 --> 00:10:26.129
One is, that he has a higher
level of brown adipose tissue

00:10:26.129 --> 00:10:28.993
or brown fat in his body,

00:10:28.993 --> 00:10:31.734
which is a heat generating
tissue in the body.

00:10:31.734 --> 00:10:34.259
Studies have shown that people
who work outside in the cold

00:10:34.259 --> 00:10:35.617
have higher levels of brown fat

00:10:35.617 --> 00:10:39.000
so it's possible that
he's able to manipulate

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.675
the level of brown fat in his body

00:10:41.675 --> 00:10:44.724
by exposure to the cold
like we're doing right now.

00:10:44.724 --> 00:10:46.984
Another theory is that he's able

00:10:46.984 --> 00:10:51.063
to secrete the hormone
noradrenaline at will

00:10:51.063 --> 00:10:55.063
through breathing and by
jumping into cold water

00:10:55.063 --> 00:10:57.089
and that adrenaline allows you

00:10:57.089 --> 00:11:00.224
to overcome coldness and illnesses.

00:11:00.224 --> 00:11:03.642
Another theory is that he
uses a form of mediation

00:11:03.642 --> 00:11:05.975
similar to the Tibetan Tummo meditation

00:11:05.975 --> 00:11:08.839
which by shutting off
the activity of the mind

00:11:08.839 --> 00:11:11.820
your metabolism gets redirected
into generating heat.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.291
It's probably a combination
of all those three

00:11:14.291 --> 00:11:18.068
and some as of yet unexplained
physiological phenomenon

00:11:18.068 --> 00:11:22.235
as well, but Wim takes it
a step further, he says,

00:11:24.077 --> 00:11:27.775
that using his method you
can go deep into the body

00:11:27.775 --> 00:11:31.889
and actually control your
own autonomic nervous system

00:11:31.889 --> 00:11:33.389
and immune system.

00:11:34.757 --> 00:11:38.999
- [Wim] I went to the
scientific scrutiny of research

00:11:38.999 --> 00:11:43.484
and put me to the test and
they saw amazing things,

00:11:43.484 --> 00:11:44.473
but then they thought,

00:11:44.473 --> 00:11:48.160
"you are the ice man, you
are just one test subject,"

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:52.037
and I said, "no what I
can do anybody can do."

00:11:52.037 --> 00:11:53.951
- You can just start doing this technique

00:11:53.951 --> 00:11:57.643
and you can modulate your
adrenaline levels by will.

00:11:57.643 --> 00:11:58.805
The stress hormones are able

00:11:58.805 --> 00:12:01.423
to modulate your immune response.

00:12:01.423 --> 00:12:03.908
There are many diseases
that are influenced

00:12:03.908 --> 00:12:05.820
by your immune system

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:07.587
and you can imagine that
it would be of interest

00:12:07.587 --> 00:12:12.503
if you could modulate that
immune response and suppress it

00:12:12.503 --> 00:12:14.047
that it might be of benefit

00:12:14.047 --> 00:12:16.672
for patients with diseases like that.

00:12:16.672 --> 00:12:19.691
- How did it feel when you
finally got recognition

00:12:19.691 --> 00:12:23.227
from the science world
that your methods worked?

00:12:23.227 --> 00:12:24.727
- I cried, really.

00:12:25.791 --> 00:12:29.348
You know what happens when your wife

00:12:29.348 --> 00:12:32.734
whom you love so dearly, she suicides,

00:12:32.734 --> 00:12:34.391
you don't understand it.

00:12:34.391 --> 00:12:38.676
You just don't understand,
you have no power any more

00:12:38.676 --> 00:12:42.336
and finally because you
have been everywhere looking

00:12:42.336 --> 00:12:45.211
for how to silence the grief,

00:12:45.211 --> 00:12:48.721
to finally get scientific recognition,

00:12:48.721 --> 00:12:50.909
that's the time when you break,

00:12:50.909 --> 00:12:53.059
that's the time when you get relief,

00:12:53.059 --> 00:12:55.861
that's the time when you can let go,

00:12:55.861 --> 00:12:57.528
that's when you cry.

00:13:00.393 --> 00:13:02.976
(upbeat music)

00:13:05.594 --> 00:13:06.790
Look at, look at the clouds.

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:08.207
- [Matt] Oh whoa.

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:12.253
Wow.
- Wow.

00:13:13.273 --> 00:13:14.690
Mother holy mama.

00:13:18.282 --> 00:13:19.115
This is nice huh?

00:13:19.115 --> 00:13:20.691
(laughing)

00:13:20.691 --> 00:13:22.996
- It's amazing what the body can do

00:13:22.996 --> 00:13:26.120
when you actually force
it to go to its limits.

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:29.120
- [Wim] Yes to it's natural ability.

00:13:33.758 --> 00:13:36.571
- We crossed the border from
Poland into the Czech Republic

00:13:36.571 --> 00:13:39.637
and now we're just about to
summit the tallest mountain

00:13:39.637 --> 00:13:42.720
in the Czech Republic, in our shorts.

00:13:46.015 --> 00:13:47.882
- Well done Matt,

00:13:47.882 --> 00:13:49.382
all the way, good.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.285
- [Matt] How are you feeling?

00:13:51.285 --> 00:13:53.549
- Ah I'm feeling good.

00:13:53.549 --> 00:13:55.132
Once again back up.

00:13:58.012 --> 00:14:00.595
(upbeat music)

00:14:04.898 --> 00:14:07.481
(wind blowing)

00:14:10.015 --> 00:14:12.975
They asked the professors
and all the scientific world,

00:14:12.975 --> 00:14:14.122
"what's happening with this guy

00:14:14.122 --> 00:14:15.753
"because this is not possible.

00:14:15.753 --> 00:14:18.467
"They're genetically the same, imprint,"

00:14:18.467 --> 00:14:21.279
my brother, and they see he is not capable

00:14:21.279 --> 00:14:24.419
of doing what he is capable of and why?

00:14:24.419 --> 00:14:26.669
Because I just dove deeper.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:31.915
It's my breathing,

00:14:31.915 --> 00:14:34.415
if we just breath more deeply,

00:14:35.474 --> 00:14:39.301
change the chemistry inside,
not shallow breathing,

00:14:39.301 --> 00:14:42.134
deep breathing, slowly but surely.

00:14:43.814 --> 00:14:46.050
This is what you do consciously.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:47.902
You do that 30 times,

00:14:47.902 --> 00:14:51.889
the chemistry in the body,
in the tissue is changing

00:14:51.889 --> 00:14:56.056
and it's changing so that the
body is becoming oxygenized,

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:01.234
alkali, and then suddenly
the brain body connection

00:15:01.234 --> 00:15:05.401
is possible by pressurizing,
by. (inhaling deeply)

00:15:09.924 --> 00:15:14.009
Once you begin to have that
connection with the body

00:15:14.009 --> 00:15:18.092
then you are able to
connect with it in the brain

00:15:18.994 --> 00:15:21.693
and that's what we do right
now with Stanford University

00:15:21.693 --> 00:15:25.599
to get rid of PTSD, fear,
trauma and depression,

00:15:25.599 --> 00:15:28.262
to learn to expand consciousness,

00:15:28.262 --> 00:15:29.950
